1020	\begin{lemma}\label{lem:qld-4-13}
1021	There exists a function $\delta_{\combine}(\eps,m,d,q) = \poly(m^2\eps,md/q)$ such that the following holds. 
1022	For every line $\line$ in
1023	$\F_q^{2m + 2}$ and $\mH \in \{ \mH_\alice,\mH_\bob\}$ there exists a POVM $\{ \hat{Q}^\line_f \}$ acting on
1024	$\mathcal{H} \otimes (\C^q)^{\otimes \nqubits}$ with outcomes $f\in
1025	\deg_{md+1}(\line)$ such that on average over a uniformly random
1026	pair $(\line, (x,z,\alpha, \beta))$ drawn from the line-point
1027	distribution over $\F_q^{2m+2}$,
